From db8a8cf0385a66e3d1378340da513efc1fde37f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Aw <zachary_aw@outlook.sg>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 08:19:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] vulkan: add GGML_OP_DSV4_ROPE_TAIL kernel

Partial ("tail") RoPE for DeepSeek-V4: the first ne0 - n_dims elements of
each row pass through unchanged; the last n_dims are rotary-embedded like a
normal/neox RoPE over an n_dims head. Reuses the shared rope push-constants
and rope_yarn(), so the math tracks the mainline RoPE shaders (and the CPU
reference within tolerance). The `inverse` op flag maps to is_back, which
negates sin while leaving cos unchanged - the same effect as the CPU
sin_sign = -1 path.

One thread per output element (wg_denoms.y == local_size_y == 256); n_nope
may be odd, so the copy region is handled element-wise and each rotated pair
is written by the thread that owns its first element. F32 and F16 variants;
supports_op mirrors the Metal gate (extended to F16 like the CPU op) plus a
contiguous-rows guard.

Wired through the generic vk_op_f32 path alongside GGML_OP_ROPE (shared
elements/dispatch branches), with a dsv4-specific push-constant builder for
the differing op_params layout, plus test-backend-ops coverage: f32/f16,
normal/neox, inverse 0/1, freq_factors, non-contiguous view, YaRN, batch,
odd n_nope, n_dims variants, and a 4096-row split. 27/27 pass on RADV
GFX1151.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
